@startuml testing
title How the plugin is tested with trmnlp-test

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Developer as dev
participant "trmnlp-test\n(gem, Docker image)" as cli
participant "test/trmnl/plugin.spec.js\n(Playwright workers)" as spec
participant "harness\n(trmnlp's own Liquid, settings\nand webhook handling)" as harness
participant "shared.liquid\n(data + layout)" as liquid
participant "Chromium page\n(device classes, palette,\ncached framework + fonts)" as page
participant "zbar" as zbar

dev -> cli : trmnlp-test [-g filter]
cli -> spec : run 114 tests in parallel
loop every test
  opt server variant
    spec -> spec : copy plugin/, patch shared.liquid the way\nTRMNL's server differs (fixed-size or sized svg,\nCRLF line endings, broken image)
  end
  spec -> harness : render({ device, view, orientation, darkMode,\nlocale, fonts, fields, webhook })
  harness -> liquid : render with the settings and the webhook "payment"
  liquid --> harness : markup
  harness -> page : open at the device's size
  page --> spec : screen
  spec -> page : locators and geometry
  note right of spec
    layout chosen = expected (rule written in the test)
    no overflow, nothing on the QR, quiet zone >= 6 px,
    QR modules >= 2 px, code fills >= 98 % of its box
    price rows right-aligned and full width, list marks,
    dividers, captions per language, title bar
  end note
  spec -> zbar : screenshot reduced to the device palette
  zbar --> spec : exact QR payload (also in dark mode)
end
cli --> dev : "114 passed" + gallery report (test/trmnl-report)

== Ship ==
dev -> dev : trmnlp lint, trmnlp push, then trmnlp pull
note right of dev
  the device is the last check: when the server shows
  something trmnlp does not, that difference becomes a
  new "server variant" test
end note
@enduml
